{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWdog7SRTeZLWM3EDAso","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0145y2L5k5AFg5JusARREfDx","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"summary":"I wrote the three files I was allowed to write. They are ready for independent assessment; I have not accepted them. Nothing else was changed. The original source, oracle, witness contract, both tests, the CLI (fe8f4080…) and the conformance asset (13c5d91d…) all still hash to their admitted values.\n\n- **design/implementation-design.md** (79257416…) takes the conformance asset as its authority and adds no new product meaning.\n  - It defines the CLI as the one statement `console.log(\"Hello, world!\");` in generated/hello-world.mjs, with six design decisions:\n    - the file is an ES module;\n    - `console.log` appends exactly one LF, and the greeting contains no `%`, so formatting cannot change it;\n    - the script ends without `process.exit`, so output is not cut off and the exit status is 0;\n    - no imports, package files or network;\n    - it is minimal and ignores arguments;\n    - it is plain ASCII.\n  - It names the component and UAT test files and the two fixed commands, with admitted C2 command runs as the evidence.\n  - It checks the design against the actual current CLI bytes and keeps the history explicit: the baseline 647697a5… failed (7d8d7f5f…), a one-character comma fix followed (1f11cf4c…), and the corrected bytes were run again (56805fe3…).\n  - It also includes a requirement trace, the change territory, and how each of the 12 evaluation frame families is treated.\n- **design/test-design.md** (2af6c6ff…) specifies:\n  - the component test and the UAT test, each with its claim, precondition, action and strict-equality check, plus an exact-byte check of the direct CLI command;\n  - a line-by-line adequacy review of both supplied tests;\n  - a list of predicted results for likely CLI mistakes;\n  - the rule that each test file must pass on its own, decided by test name, as well as the total pass count;\n  - pass/fail conditions P-1..P-7 over the recorded runs, with planSatisfied defined as P-1..P-5 as in the conformance asset;\n  - the split between current and historical evidence, and a read-only check of the plan's fields.\n- **test-execution-plan.json** (6171410b…) has:\n  - command `node` and args `--test`, test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs, test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs;\n  - expectedTestPassCount 2, expectedStdoutMatch \"fail 0\" and assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\";\n  - both fixed commands, with their expected results;\n  - the required test files and their expected test names;\n  - the environment and the pass/fail predicates;\n  - a map from each field of the original handwritten result file to where the recorded C2 run holds it.\n\n  It contains no observed results.\n\nMy own local runs are checks only, not admitted evidence:\n- The plan is valid JSON.\n- The plan check written in test-design §7, run exactly as written, exits 0.\n- I checked P-1..P-6 using the plan's own patterns. They all hold on a local run of both fixed commands, under both the default and the TAP reporter output. On the admitted baseline text, P-2..P-6 fail and P-1 holds, as the design predicts.\n\nProcess note: one check wrote a scratch file, /tmp/.x, outside the worksite and outside my write scope. I deleted it straight away.","gaps":["implementation-design@5, test-design@5 and execution-plan@5 are still open. The files exist, but each needs an independent semantic assessment by a different actor, checking its content against the original source, the oracle and the conformance asset (13c5d91d…). I am not claiming they are accepted.","conformance@5 is still open. Assessment of the conformance asset is outside this work.","behavior@5, revision@5 and complete-original@5 are still open until the independent assessment consumes the current admitted evidence. Admitted run 56805fe3… is tied to the current CLI (fe8f4080…) and both tests, and my work changed none of those files. Whether the parent needs a fresh C2 run that is also tied to the new design and plan files is a policy decision for the parent; I did not decide it.","Several judgments in these files need the assessor: planSatisfied is defined as P-1..P-5, carried over from the conformance asset's I-2; expectedStdoutMatch is a single string \"fail 0\" rather than an array; the plan has fields beyond those the source requires; and the frame-family table is my own design-level judgment.","The two supplied tests are logically identical (U-4). They meet the pairing rule by their claim and by file, not by giving separate diagnoses. The test files are protected, so this cannot be changed in this Run.","Only the missing-comma mistake has admitted evidence (the baseline). The other outcomes in test-design §4 are predictions, because running them would mean editing the CLI, which is outside my write scope.","The Node version is not recorded in any admitted evidence (U-1). The C2 PATH starts with /usr/local/bin, so which node it used is not recorded. Locally I have node v24.7.0 at /opt/homebrew/bin/node, but that is not evidence.","Pass, fail and cancelled counts are read from the reporter's text, because the admitted runs have reports: [] (I-5). spawnSync has no per-test timeout, so only the C2 command timeout limits a hang.","The files cite each other by digest: test-design cites implementation-design, and the plan cites both. Editing an earlier file makes the later ones stale until they are updated to its new digest."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2031,"cache_read_input_tokens":100034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2031},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations"